rl":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-13T05:35:28Z","updated_at":"2025-06-13T06:07:27Z","body":">It would be very useful to bisect if you can.\n\nThis is a regression from #101941.\n\n>Also when I save global uniform texture and reload the project, the texture isn't saved and becomes empty.\n\nIt's a separate issue. Actually, `project.godot` never saves embedded resources, it only stores resource paths:\n```\n[shader_globals]\n\ntex_arr={\n\"type\": \"sampler2DArray\",\n\"value\": \"\"\n}\ntex={\n\"type\": \"sampler2D\",\n\"value\": \"res://new_gradient_texture_2d.tres\"\n}\n```\nSo embedded resources will be quietly lost after reloading, unless they are saved to paths. it can also be reproduced in 4.4. A possible solution is displaying a warning when there are unsaved resources in global shader uniform.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2969116354/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]